      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Incorporating a more predatory or animalistic nature into the tribal setting can indeed amplify their perceived threat to the empire. This could manifest in extreme combat behavior, where their instincts drive them to attack without hesitation. They might exhibit little to no mercy towards enemies, showing raw and visceral forms of violence. In crowds or communities, these tribespeople might prioritize strength and dominance, leading to aggressive interactions, territorial disputes, and an environment of constant strife. This could highlight a stark contrast with the empire, which ostensibly values refined laws, diplomacy, and a structured society anchored in empathy and restraint. By shaping these tribespeople through such lenses, you vividly underscore their primal nature and inherent discord with the more civilized empire.",
      "source": "target",
