      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a really intense direction for them. to make it feel even more grounded in the world-building, i want to look at how this 'predatory' nature affects their actual biology or even their sense of self. if they're so driven by these base urges and instincts, does it feel like they're almost a different subspecies or something? like, would they have certain physical traits—maybe things like sharper teeth, different eye structures, or even a different way of smelling or sensing things—that make them feel less like 'people' and more like a distinct, more primal species compared to the empire's citizens?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
